cartridge "MUTANT BREAKOUT/FUNKNFLOW5200/2026"

' MUTANT BREAKOUT
' A side-scrolling beat 'em up. Genetic experiments break out of Facility 7:
' fight through the Cell Block, the Sewers and the Perimeter, one boss each.
'
' Controls (either joystick): stick = walk (left/right) and move in the lane
' (up/down); LEFT button = attack (tap for a 3-hit combo; in the air, a flying
' kick); RIGHT button = jump. The keypad is not used. On the title screen the
' stick picks the mutant (left/right) and the menu (up/down); a button confirms.
'
' The mutants: SCALES (lizard: balanced), TUSK (boar: slow, hits hard, tough),
' FLUTTER (moth: fast, high jumps, fragile).
'
' Liberties / design notes: original game, inspired by the arcade beat 'em ups
' of the late 1980s. The screen locks for each wave of guards, scientists with
' tranquilizer darts and hounds; when it is clear, GO points right and the
' corridor scrolls (the wall at half the speed of the floor). One player. The
' stage art is periodic strips whose pattern bits are rotated each frame
' (smooth pixel scrolling on the TMS9918; see scroll.asm).

const THpf = 128
const THpe = 129
const TBsf = 130
const TBse = 131
